```cpp
CtxIOut = PHI->getIncomingBlock(*U)->getTerminator();
```

This sets `CtxIOut` unconditionally. But what if `ValOut == PHI` (line 598)? In that case, we return early (line 599) and `CtxIOut` is uninitialized! The caller expects `CtxIOut` to be set, but it won't be.

Actually, looking at the caller in `computeKnownBitsFromOperator`:

```cpp
